 ## Overview
-This method initializes the bias terms of the final neural network layers in radiance field optimization to ensure the model starts with low density and high transmittance. It sets the bias to the midpoint of predefined log-space bounds for density and temperature, preventing early saturation and stabilizing the initial training phase [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Low-density initialization](4670-low-density-initialization.md) by providing a specific, bounded strategy for determining that initial bias value.
+This method initializes the bias term of the final layer in a neural radiance field (NeRF) network to the midpoint of the log-space bounds for density and temperature. By setting the initial output to the center of the valid range, it ensures that the predicted alpha values are low, effectively starting the optimization with a transparent scene [S1, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods like Alpha Invariance Initialization by explicitly targeting the log-space parameters rather than relying on alpha-invariance constraints [S1, unofficial].
 
